          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em relative
            monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \colon A \to E
            is much like a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            except that its underlying functor is not required to be an
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit"} unit
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \colon A \to E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is a monad
            %em relative to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
          %p
            Ordinary monads are the special case of
            = succeed "-relative" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+functor"} identity functor
          %p
            In generalisation of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "monad#RelationBetweenAdjunctionsAndMonads"} relation between adjunctions and monads
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+adjunctions"} relative adjunctions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+comonads"} relative comonads
            are related to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+coadjunctions"} relative coadjunctions
          %h2#Definition Definitions
