          %p
            In particular, in the special case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            is the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+functor"} identity functor
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#def"}
            reduces to the definition of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad+in+extension+form"} monad in extension form
          %h3#as_monoids_in_a_skewmonoidal_category_skewmulticategory_or_multicategory As monoids in a skew-monoidal category, skew-multicategory, or multicategory
          %p
            Monads are, by definition,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoids"} monoids
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctors"} endofunctors
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \colon A \to E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [A, E]
            may frequently be equipped with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skew-monoidal+category"} skew-monoidal
            structure. The notion of a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skew-monoidal+category"} skew-monoidal category
            is like that of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            except that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitors"} unitors
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associators"} associators
            are not necessarily
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invertible+morphism"} invertible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} Monoids
            may be defined in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skew-monoidal+category"} skew-monoidal category
            analogously as to in a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [A, E]
            (equipped with the skew-monoidal structure induced by
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            = succeed "-relative" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a{:href => "#ACU15"}> ACU15, Thm. 3.4
                )
              %br/
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \colon A \to E
              be a functor for which
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Lan
                      %mi J
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Lan}_J \colon [A, E] \to [E, E]
              exists (e.g. if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is small and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              cocomplete). Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [A, E]
              admtis a skew-monoidal structure, with unit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              and tensor
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %msup
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi J
                      %mi G
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Lan
                        %mi J
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \circ^J G = (\mathrm{Lan}_J F) \circ G
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mi J
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ([A, E], J, \circ^J)
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \colon A \to E
            is a free completion of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            under a class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℱ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
            of small colimits, then this skew-monoidal structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [A, E]
            is properly monoidal, since it is equivalent to the
            = succeed "-colimit" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to E
            = succeed "-colimit" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %p
            More generally, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
